POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "To Kill a Mockingbird",
  "stock": 8
}


### Verification: and check JSON response for lowStock property.
# Expected Outcome: Each book in the response includes lowStock:
# true if stock < 10, otherwise false.

GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books


### Exercise 8: Business Logic and Actions (OData # Basics - OData Actions)
# Action
# Expected Outcome: Stock decreases by the ordered quantity, and
# success message is returned.
# Verification: Check Books entity before and after the action to
# confirm stock reduction.

POST http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/submitOrder
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "book": "2",
  "quantity": 2
}


# Exercise 9: Filtering and Querying (OData # Basics - OData Queries)
# Expected Outcome: Only books with stock less than 10 are returned.
# Test the following queries in your browser or REST client:
### 1. Filter by stock:   

GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books?$filter=stock lt 10

### 2. Sort by title:
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books?$orderby=title asc

### 3. Select specific fields:
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books?$select=title,stock

### 4. Expand associations:
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books?$expand=author

### 5. Count records:
GET http://localhost:4004/odata/v4/catalog/Books/$count


# Expected Outcome: Each query returns filtered, sorted, or projected
# data as expected.
# Exercise 9: Filtering and Querying (OData
# Basics)
# Verification: Compare results with full dataset to confirm query
# behavior.